  "id": "injunctive-norm",
  "term": "injunctive norm",
  "definition": "An injunctive norm is a social norm based on what people believe ought to be done or is morally appropriate in a situation. It reflects perceived social expectations about proper behavior, rather than beliefs about what most people actually do.",
